### CLI Help Text

Help text is documentation. Make it useful:

```go
var installCmd = &cobra.Command{
    Use:   "install",
    Short: "Install suparship components to a Kubernetes cluster",
    Long: `Install suparship components to a Kubernetes cluster.

This command installs ArgoCD, Kargo, and supporting components based on
the selected profile. The cluster must be accessible via kubectl.

Profiles:
  demo    Full local setup with k3d, sample apps (default for 'suparship demo')
  core    Minimal: ArgoCD + Kargo + ingress
  full    Everything: core + monitoring stack

After installation, access points will be displayed.`,
    Example: `  # Install core components
  suparship install --profile=core

  # Install to specific context
  suparship install --profile=core --context=my-cluster

  # Preview without installing
  suparship install --profile=demo --dry-run`,
}
```

## Keeping Docs Updated

### PR Checklist Item

Every PR with user-facing changes MUST update docs:

- [ ] README updated if behavior changed
- [ ] Help text updated if flags changed
- [ ] Examples updated if commands changed

### Automated Checks

```yaml
# .github/workflows/docs.yaml
- name: Verify README examples work
  run: |
    # Extract code blocks from README and verify they're valid
    ./scripts/verify-readme-examples.sh
    
- name: Check for outdated version references
  run: |
    # Ensure version numbers in docs match code
    grep -r "v[0-9]\+\.[0-9]\+\.[0-9]\+" docs/ | \
      grep -v "$(cat VERSION)" && exit 1 || true
```

